  "instance_extraction": [
    {
      "entity_or_property": "abstract",
      "value": "  Paul Erdos asked how frequently the ternary expansion of 2^n omits the digit\n2. He conjectured this happens only for finitely many values of n. We\ngeneralize this question to consider iterates of two discrete dynamical\nsystems. The first is over the real numbers, and considers the integer part of\nlambda 2^n for a real input lambda. The second is over the 3-adic integers, and\nconsiders the sequence lambda 2^n for a 3-adic integer input lambda.\n  We show that the number of input values that have infinitely many iterates\nomitting the digit 2 in their ternary expansion is small in a suitable sense.\nFor each nonzero input we give an asymptotic upper bound on the number of the\nfirst k iterates that omit the digit 2, as k goes to infinity. We also study\nauxiliary problems concerning the Hausdorff dimension of intersections of\nmultiplicative translates of 3-adic Cantor sets.\n",
      "entity_type": "Article"
    },
    {
      "entity_or_property": "name",
      "value": "k",
      "entity_type": "Keyword"
    }
  ],
  "relation_mapping": [
    {
      "source_node": "Article",
      "relation": "HAS_KEY",
      "target_node": "Keyword",
      "direction": "OUTGOING"
    }
  ],
  "validation_check": {
    "status": "PASS",
    "description": "The Cypher query accurately matches Article nodes with the specified abstract property and finds connected Keyword nodes whose name starts with 'k' via the HAS_KEY relationship."
  },
  "cypher": "MATCH (a:Article)-[:HAS_KEY]->(k:Keyword)\nWHERE a.abstract = \"  Paul Erdos asked how frequently the ternary expansion of 2^n omits the digit\\n2. He conjectured this happens only for finitely many values of n. We\\ngeneralize this question to consider iterates of two discrete dynamical\\nsystems. The first is over the real numbers, and considers the integer part of\\nlambda 2^n for a real input lambda. The second is over the 3-adic integers, and\\nconsiders the sequence lambda 2^n for a 3-adic integer input lambda.\\n  We show that the number of input values that have infinitely many iterates\\nomitting the digit 2 in their ternary expansion is small in a suitable sense.\\nFor each nonzero input we give an asymptotic upper bound on the number of the\\nfirst k iterates that omit the digit 2, as k goes to infinity. We also study\\nauxiliary problems concerning the Hausdorff dimension of intersections of\\nmultiplicative translates of 3-adic Cantor sets.\\n\" AND k.name STARTS WITH 'k'\nRETURN k"
}

